# Dependencies — no new packages without approval

## Context

`app/package.json` currently depends only on TypeScript and vitest tooling.
This is a deliberately small, dependency-free sample app (custom store, custom
text lib) — pulling in a library to "solve" something the app already does
itself (state management, string helpers, UUIDs, etc.) works against the
exercise, per `materials/architecture-brief.md`.

## Rule

- Do NOT add a new entry to `app/package.json` `dependencies` or
  `devDependencies` unless the user explicitly asks for that package by name
  in the current request.
- Prefer solving problems with what's already in `app/src` (the store,
  reducer, selectors, `lib/text.ts`) or with plain TypeScript/Node built-ins.
- If a dependency genuinely seems necessary, say so and ask before installing
  it — don't run `npm install` silently.

## How to verify

1. `git diff app/package.json app/package-lock.json` — empty, unless the user
   explicitly requested a specific package in this session.
2. No `npm install <pkg>` was run without the user naming `<pkg>` first.
